Build a complete, modern, responsive Web 2.0 travel information website inspired by the purpose and content style of https://travelobliss.com/.

IMPORTANT:
- Create an original website for a Web 2.0 publishing platform. Do not copy the exact website design, text, images, branding assets, or source code from Travelobliss.
- The website should be related to air travel, airline information, flight guidance, destination inspiration, and practical travel planning.
- Use original wording and royalty-free or placeholder images.
- Make the site useful to readers first. Avoid keyword stuffing, misleading booking claims, fake reviews, or thin duplicate content.

BRAND AND POSITIONING
Use the site name: Travel Guide Hub (the name can be changed later).
Position it as an independent travel information resource that helps readers understand airline policies, prepare for flights, explore destinations, and plan journeys with confidence.
If mentioning Travelobliss, describe it accurately as an airline-focused travel information website offering flight guidance, route information, travel tips, and helpful resources. Do not imply that this Web 2.0 site is the official Travelobliss website or an airline.

DESIGN DIRECTION
- Premium, clean, friendly travel aesthetic.
- Use a navy-blue, sky-blue, and white colour palette with restrained bright-blue accents.
- Use readable modern typography, generous spacing, rounded cards, subtle shadows, and clear navigation.
- Use a large travel hero section with an airplane / airport / destination visual.
- Ensure the design works well on mobile, tablet, and desktop.
- Add accessible colour contrast, descriptive image alt text, and visible keyboard focus states.

SITE STRUCTURE
1. Home page
   - Header with logo/site name and navigation.
   - Hero headline: “Travel Smarter with Helpful Airline Guides and Travel Tips”.
   - Short introduction explaining the site's independent travel-information purpose.
   - Featured sections for Airline Guides, Flight Tips, Destination Guides, and Travel Planning.
   - Recent articles section with cards and short summaries.
   - Clear footer with About, Contact, Privacy Policy, and Disclaimer links.

2. About page
   - Explain the site's purpose and editorial approach.
   - State that airline policies can change and readers should confirm important details with the airline before travel.

3. Airline Guides
   - Create article templates for topics such as baggage guidance, check-in information, seat selection, missed flights, schedule changes, and travelling with children.
   - Do not invent airline policy details, fees, age limits, or deadlines. Use placeholders or clearly mark facts that need verification against the airline's official website.

4. Destination Guides
   - Create destination cards and article templates for cities such as Paris, London, Rome, Barcelona, and Amsterdam.
   - Include practical planning tips, highlights, and links to related travel resources.

5. Travel Tips
   - Include useful checklists and explainers about airport preparation, documents, packing, connecting flights, and group travel.

6. Contact and legal pages
   - Add editable Contact, Privacy Policy, and Disclaimer pages.
   - Do not invent a physical address, phone number, or email address. Use clearly labelled placeholders until real contact details are supplied.

CONTENT REQUIREMENTS
- Write clear, natural, original English.
- Use one H1 per page, logical H2/H3 headings, concise paragraphs, and descriptive internal links.
- Add SEO-friendly page titles and meta descriptions without keyword stuffing.
- Use meaningful URLs/slugs and descriptive image alt text.
- Add Article structured data only where appropriate and only with accurate author, date, and article information.
- Include a visible editorial note that airline rules and travel requirements may change.
- Avoid claiming to compare live fares, book tickets, or provide airline customer support unless those functions genuinely exist.

TECHNICAL REQUIREMENTS
- Generate a complete static website using HTML5, CSS3, and lightweight JavaScript.
- Include all necessary files: index.html, about.html, airline-guides.html, destinations.html, travel-tips.html, contact.html, disclaimer.html, privacy.html, style.css, and script.js.
- Use semantic HTML and reusable CSS components.
- Make navigation links work and ensure there are no broken internal links.
- Add a mobile navigation menu, responsive article cards, and a functional contact form layout with a clear note if no backend is connected.
- Keep code organised, commented where helpful, and ready to publish with GitHub Pages.
- Include a README.md with simple instructions for uploading the files to a GitHub repository and enabling GitHub Pages.

SEO AND WEB 2.0 PUBLISHING GUIDANCE
- Treat this as a standalone informational publication, not a doorway page made only to link to Travelobliss.
- If a Travelobliss reference is contextually useful, include at most a natural, transparent editorial link such as “For additional airline-focused travel information, visit Travelobliss” linking to https://travelobliss.com/.
- Do not repeat the same backlink in every paragraph or create keyword-rich anchor spam.
- Publish genuinely useful, original articles and disclose any relationship or ownership if applicable.
- Do not create fake author biographies, fake testimonials, or fabricated expertise.

DELIVERABLE
Return the complete website source code, with each file clearly labelled and its full contents provided. Make the project ready for direct upload to GitHub. Also provide a short README explaining exactly which files to create, where to paste each code section, and how to publish the website using GitHub Pages.
